  the worker's first `{type:'progress', value:0}` message, let alone
  `'done'`. Confirmed this is not vectorizer-specific and not opencv-related
  at all by running the QuickJS project's own pristine, unmodified
  `tests/test_worker.js` + `tests/test_worker_module.js` (from
  `/mnt/data/Projects/plot-cv/quickjs/tests/`, no opencv import anywhere) -
  it hangs identically, with zero messages delivered in either direction
  (parent->worker or worker->parent), even after uncommenting the test's
  own diagnostic `print()` calls. `os.Worker` threads are actually spawned
  (visible as real OS threads via `ps -T` on a running process) but
  `parent.postMessage()`/`worker.postMessage()` never triggers the other
  side's `onmessage`. Machine has several other quickjs source checkouts
  under `/mnt/data/Projects/quickjs-*` and `/mnt/data/Projects/plot-cv/quickjs/quickjs-*`
  (2024-01-13, 2025-04-26, 2025-09-13, 2026-06-04) - worth trying a rebuild
